Accept `.duckdb_extension.wasm` as the valid extension filename suffix
when the engine is compiled with WASM_LOADABLE_EXTENSIONS. The engine's
strict check throws PermissionException for anything not ending in
`.duckdb_extension`, but Haybarn's wasm extension distribution uses
the `.duckdb_extension.wasm` suffix (each file IS a WebAssembly
module — `.duckdb_extension` is the application convention,
`.wasm` is the file format).

Companion to the suffix changes upstream all_of_them.patch already
makes to `duckdb_extensions.cpp`, `extension_helper.cpp`, and
`extension_install.cpp` — those flip the filename construction to
`.duckdb_extension.wasm`; this extends the same convention to the
load-side validation.

diff --git a/src/main/extension/extension_load.cpp b/src/main/extension/extension_load.cpp
--- a/src/main/extension/extension_load.cpp
+++ b/src/main/extension/extension_load.cpp
@@ -453,9 +453,9 @@
 		direct_load = true;
 		filename = fs.ExpandPath(filename);
 	}
-	if (!StringUtil::EndsWith(filename, ".duckdb_extension")) {
+	if (!StringUtil::EndsWith(filename, ".duckdb_extension.wasm")) {
 		throw PermissionException(
-		    "Haybarn extensions are files ending with '.duckdb_extension', loading different "
+		    "Haybarn extensions are files ending with '.duckdb_extension.wasm', loading different "
 		    "files is not possible, error while loading from '%s', consider 'INSTALL <path>; LOAD <name>;'",
 		    filename);
 	}
